           ating systems are known to generate fragmented packets with the
           _d_o_n_t_-_f_r_a_g_m_e_n_t bit set.  This is particularly true with NFS.  _S_c_r_u_b
           will drop such fragmented _d_o_n_t_-_f_r_a_g_m_e_n_t packets unless _n_o_-_d_f is
           specified.

           Unfortunately some operating systems also generate their
           _d_o_n_t_-_f_r_a_g_m_e_n_t packets with a zero IP identification field.  Clear‐
           ing the _d_o_n_t_-_f_r_a_g_m_e_n_t bit on packets with a zero IP ID may cause
           deleterious results if an upstream router later fragments the
