           The packet is matched.  This mechanism is used to provide fine
           grained filtering without altering the block/pass state of a
           packet.  _m_a_t_c_h rules differ from _b_l_o_c_k and _p_a_s_s rules in that pa‐
           rameters are set for every rule a packet matches, not only on the
           last matching rule.  For the following parameters, this means that
           the parameter effectively becomes "sticky" until explicitly over‐
           ridden: _q_u_e_u_e, _d_n_p_i_p_e, _d_n_q_u_e_u_e, _r_t_a_b_l_e, _s_c_r_u_b

